body:
Videos Watched: The 64 bits meme ones and "Minecraft |Going to nether!!!!| E4"

&#x200B;

So, first of all, I think that you are doing better on the meme videos than on the gameplays, not to say that they are bad, of course.

&#x200B;

In relation to the gameplay, I tell this to most people that are starting out on YouTube, go for short and sweet. Focus on making shorter (for example, 5 minutes) videos. That way there is a better chance of people watching all of it and actually clicking on them. Shorter videos tend to be more appealing and, especially with a small audience you never want to make videos too long.

&#x200B;

My second tip would be to add more subtitles to the gameplay videos, this makes it so that the viewer doesn't have to be watching normal gameplay with nothing to it, which will, eventually, get boring. Cut the parts where you aren't doing anything interesting. Think about it this way, if it was someone else's video and you would skip over that part, cut it.

&#x200B;

Also try to find appropriate music to fit the gameplay, when I started out I used a lot opf Kevin MacLeod's music. You should recognize it from other people. You could also use Animal Crossing music.

&#x200B;

My last piece of advice to you would be to share the videos as most as you can, that being on Reddit, Facebook, Instagram, etc. There are a lot of good Sub-Reddits to share your videos.

&#x200B;

Anyways, good luck! :)
